      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part I, Line 2:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ACCEF SCHOLARSHIP COMMITTEE REVIEWS THE WRITTEN APPLICATIONS AND APPROVES THE GRANTS OR SCHOLARSHIP AWARDS BY ISSUING A LETTER TO THE APPROVED CANDIDATES. AFTER ACCEF RECEIVES THE NOTICE OF ACCEPTANCE FROM THE APPROVED CANDIDATES, THE AWARDS, GRANTS OR SPONSORSHIP FUNDS ARE DISBURSED THROUGH ACCEF VOLUNTEERS TO THE SCHOOLS OR APPROPRIATE ORGANIZATION TO PAY APPROVED STUDENT TUITION. MOST OF THE FUNDS ARE NOT DISBURSED DIRECTLY TO STUDENTS AND SEPARATELY DISBURSED FOR EACH SCHOOL SEMESTER. RECEIPTS FROM THE SCHOOLS ARE OBTAINED BY THE VOLUNTEERS. THE ACCEF VOLUNTEERS CLOSELY MONITOR THE USAGE TO ENSURE THE FUNDS ARE USED FOR THE PURPOSES GRANTED BY ACCEF.</ExplanationTxt>
